":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11114445492,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSuNQNs8AAAAClnj6tA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vansh-09/BountyScout/labels/bounty-alert","name":"bounty-alert","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-07T06:50:13Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:50:13Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Active Bounty Scan Results\n\n**Scan Time:** 2026-07-07 06:50 UTC\n\n#### 1. [Add is-cjk-radical-lame-four-present API utility](https://github.com/xevrion-v2/agent-playground/issues/5844)\n- **Repository:** [xevrion-v2/agent-playground](https://github.com/xevrion-v2/agent-playground)\n- **Comments:** 2\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-07-07T06:49:51Z\n\n#### 2. [Add frame-ancestors/X-Frame-Options + baseline security headers (route-aware, hub-safe)](https://github.com/ima-jin/imajin-ai/issues/1247)\n- **Repository:** [ima-jin/imajin-ai](https://github.com/ima-jin/imajin-ai)\n- **Comments:** 0\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-07-07T06:49:25Z\n\n#### 3. [🎯 Bounty Alert: 5 New Opportunityies found](https://github.com/freedom-winds/BountyScout/issues/15)\n- **Repository:** [freedom-winds/BountyScout](https://github.com/freedom-winds/BountyScout)\n- **Comments:** 0\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-07-07T06:47:42Z\n\n#### 4. [Add LinkedIn integration](https://github.com/corsairdev/corsair/issues/385)\n- **Repository:** [corsairdev/corsair](https://github.com/corsairdev/corsair)\n- **Comments:** 0\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-07-07T06:39:52Z\n\n#### 5. [keras-3.8.0-py3-none-any.whl: 12 vulnerabilities (highest severity is: 9.0)](https://github.com/rsoreq-mend/tensorflow/issues/35)\n- **Repository:** [rsoreq-mend/tensorflow](https://github.com/rsoreq-mend/tensorflow)\n- **Comments:** 0\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-07-07T06:36:26Z\n\n#### 6. [keras-3.10.0-py3-none-any.whl: 11 vulnerabilities (highest severity is: 9.0)](https://github.com/rsoreq-mend/tensorflow/issues/25)\n- **Repository:** [rsoreq-mend/tensorflow](https://github.com/rsoreq-mend/tensorflow)\n- **Comments:** 0\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-07-07T06:36:24Z\n\n#### 7. [[zero-bounty][agent-friendly] Fix frontmatter: agent-memory-extractor-timing.md](https://github.com/Ikalus1988/MisakaNet/issues/376)\n- **Repository:** [Ikalus1988/MisakaNet](https://github.com/Ikalus1988/MisakaNet)\n- **Comments:** 0\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-07-07T06:30:39Z\n\n#### 8. [Test important GPIO initialization in CI (libpanda)](https://github.com/commaai/panda/issues/2203)\n- **Repository:** [commaai/panda](https://github.com/commaai/panda)\n- **Comments:** 4\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-07-07T06:21:56Z\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vansh-09/BountyScout/issues/288/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vansh-09/BountyScout/issues/288/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ima-jin/imajin-ai/issues/1247","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ima-jin/imajin-ai","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ima-jin/imajin-ai/issues/1247/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ima-jin/imajin-ai/issues/1247/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ima-jin/imajin-ai/issues/1247/events","html_url":"https://github.com/ima-jin/imajin-ai/issues/1247","id":4826006099,"node_id":"I_kwDOROPgcM8AAAABH6cCUw","number":1247,"title":"Add frame-ancestors/X-Frame-Options + baseline security headers (route-aware, hub-safe)","user":{"login":"imajin-jin","id":262684899,"node_id":"U_kgDOD6hA4w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262684899?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/imajin-jin","html_url":"https://github.com/imajin-jin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imajin-jin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imajin-jin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imajin-jin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imajin-jin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imajin-jin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imajin-jin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imajin-jin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imajin-jin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imajin-jin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11371850744,"node_id":"LA_kwDOROPgcM8AAAACpdCr-A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ima-jin/imajin-ai/labels/active","name":"active","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"Being worked now"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-07T06:49:25Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:49:25Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Summary\n\nAdd framing/clickjacking protection (`frame-ancestors` CSP + `X-Frame-Options` fallback) and baseline security headers across the platform — done **route-aware** so it doesn't break the auth hub's embedded service iframes.\n\nPrompted by an external report flagging that `https://jin.imajin.ai/auth/login` returns no `X-Frame-Options`/CSP and is framable. The report's threat list is inflated beg-bounty boilerplate; the underlying finding (missing frame protection on login) is a legitimate, low-severity hardening item worth fixing properly.\n\n## Verified current state (prod)\n\n- `jin.imajin.ai/auth/login` → `200`, **no** `X-Frame-Options`, **no** `Content-Security-Policy`.\n- Same across `imajin.ai`, `auth.`, `chat.`, `profile.`, `events.` — Caddy is the front door; **no service sets frame headers**.\n\n## Why a naive global `frame-ancestors 'none'` is WRONG\n\nWe frame our own surfaces. A blanket deny breaks the product:\n\n- `apps/kernel/app/auth/components/ServiceEmbed.tsx` — the **auth hub** iframes service dashboards at `${SERVICE_URL}/dashboard?embed=hub&did=...`. Consumers: `apps/kernel/app/auth/{events,market,coffee,dykil,links,learn,pay,media}/page.tsx`. Cross-subdomain (e.g. `events.imajin.ai` inside `auth.imajin.ai`) plus same-origin (`pay`, `media`).\n- `apps/events/app/e/[eventId]/survey-accordion.tsx` — embeds a survey iframe with `postMessage` origin validation.\n- `apps/kernel/app/auth/attestations/components/DocumentViewer.tsx` — iframes own media assets (PDF/text).\n- `apps/learn/.../[lessonId]/page.tsx` — iframes an **external** `videoUrl` (outbound only; irrelevant to our `frame-ancestors` policy, but don't accidentally CSP-block the video with a `frame-src` rule).\n\nSo framed-*by-us* services need permissive `frame-ancestors`; auth/login (never framed internally) should hard-deny.\n\n## Approach — route-aware CSP in the app layer (NOT blanket Caddy)\n\nThe auth app serves **both** the login page (want deny) and embedded `pay`/`media` paths (want allow) from the **same origin** — a vhost-level Caddy header can't split them. Set framing CSP where routes are known.\n\n### Tier 1 — hard deny (never framed)\nLogin + auth-sensitive credential pages:\n- `Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'`\n- `X-Frame-Options: DENY`\n\n### Tier 2 — allow Imajin origins (framed by the hub)\nService dashboards / survey / document routes:\n- `Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self' https://*.imajin.ai https://imajin.ai`\n- **No `X-Frame-Options`** (XFO can't express an allow-list; `SAMEORIGIN` would break cross-subdomain framing — CSP does the work).\n\n### Tier 3 — baseline hardening (everywhere, safe)\nCheap to add at Caddy for all vhosts:\n- `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`\n- `Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin`\n\n## Implementation notes\n\n- Prefer per-app Next.js `headers()` (or middleware) for the framing tiers — kernel `next.config.js` currently has **no** `headers()`, so it's greenfield.\n- Consider a shared helper in a package (e.g. `@imajin/*` security-headers util) so all `apps/*` apply Tier 2/3 consistently rather than copy-paste — matches the shared-component convention.\n- Confirm whether `jin.` and `auth.` are the same kernel app behind different vhosts; apply Tier 1 to whichever host serves `/auth/login`.\n- Watch for **duplicate CSP headers** (app-set + any future Caddy-set) — browsers intersect multiple CSPs, which can silently over-restrict. Keep framing CSP in exactly one layer.\n- If `learn` gets a CSP with `frame-src`, allow the external video origins or the lesson video breaks.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `curl -I https://jin.imajin.ai/auth/login` returns `frame-ancestors 'none'` and `X-Frame-Options: DENY`.\n- [ ] The auth hub still renders embedded dashboards (events/market/coffee/dykil/links/pay/media) with no console CSP frame errors.\n- [ ] Event survey embed and attestation DocumentViewer still render.\n- [ ] `learn` external video iframe still plays.\n- [ ] Tier 3 baseline headers present on all vhosts.\n- [ ] No duplicate/conflicting CSP headers on any route.\n\n## Out of scope / do not\n\n- No reply or bounty payment to the reporter (Alpha Inferno / \"Olivia\").\n- Not a full CSP `script-src`/`default-src` lockdown — this ticket is framing + baseline only. A full CSP is a separate, larger effort.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ima-jin/imajin-ai/issues/1247/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ima-jin/imajin-ai/issues/1247/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/freedom-winds/BountyScout/issues/15","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/freedom-winds/BountyScout","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/freedom-winds/BountyScout/issues/15/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/freedom-winds/BountyScout/issues/15/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/freedom-winds/BountyScout/issues/15/events","html_url":"https://github.com/freedom-winds/BountyScout/issues/15","id":4825996719,"node_id":"I_kwDOTOXMzs8AAAABH6bdrw","number":15,"title":"🎯 Bounty Alert: 5 New Opportunityies found","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11425538388,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTOXMzs8AAAACqQPhVA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/freedom-winds/BountyScout/labels/bounty-alert","name":"bounty-alert","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-07T06:47:42Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:47:42Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Active Bounty Scan Results\n\n**Scan Time:** 2026-07-07 06:47 UTC\n\n#### 1. [🎯 Fix: Request body is exhausted and sent empty on automatic retries when using io.Reader / io.ReadCloser](https://github.com/xoufygqamm4/resty/issues/1)\n- **Repository:** [xoufygqamm4/resty](https://github.com/xoufygqamm4/resty)\n- **Comments:** 2\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-07-07T06:47:06Z\n\n#### 2. [Add LinkedIn integration](https://github.com/corsairdev/corsair/issues/385)\n- **Repository:** [corsairdev/corsair](https://github.com/corsairdev/corsair)\n- **Comments:** 0\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-07-07T06:39:52Z\n\n#### 3. [keras-3.8.0-py3-none-any.whl: 12 vulnerabilities (highest severity is: 9.0)](https://github.com/rsoreq-mend/tensorflow/issues/35)\n- **Repository:** [rsoreq-mend/tensorflow](https://github.com/rsoreq-mend/tensorflow)\n- **Comments:** 0\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-07-07T06:36:26Z\n\n#### 4. [keras-3.10.0-py3-none-any.whl: 11 vulnerabilities (highest severity is: 9.0)](https://github.com/rsoreq-mend/tensorflow/issues/25)\n- **Repository:** [rsoreq-mend/tensorflow](https://github.com/rsoreq-mend/tensorflow)\n- **Comments:** 0\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-07-07T06:36:24Z\n\n#### 5. [[zero-bounty][agent-friendly] Fix frontmatter: agent-memory-extractor-timing.md](https://github.com/Ikalus1988/MisakaNet/issues/376)\n- **Repository:** [Ikalus1988/MisakaNet](https://github.com/Ikalus1988/MisakaNet)\n- **Comments:** 0\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-07-07T06:30:39Z\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/freedom-winds/BountyScout/issues/15/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/freedom-winds/BountyScout/issues/15/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/issues/3","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/issues/3/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/issues/3/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/issues/3/events","html_url":"https://github.com/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/issues/3","id":3568021352,"node_id":"I_kwDOQLu5pc7Uq69o","number":3,"title":"Slippage Sentinel","user":{"login":"ponderingdemocritus","id":90423308,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNDIzMzA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90423308?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus","html_url":"https://github.com/ponderingdemocritus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9550858602,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQLu5pc8AAAACOUaJag","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":9550858603,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQLu5pc8AAAACOUaJaw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/labels/defi","name":"defi","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":9550859097,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQLu5pc8AAAACOUaLWQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/labels/risk-management","name":"risk-management","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":9550883116,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQLu5pc8AAAACOUbpLA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/labels/$1000","name":"$1000","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":99,"created_at":"2025-10-29T21:45:21Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:43:44Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Purpose\nEstimate safe slippage tolerance for any route to prevent swap reverts.\n\n## Specification\n\n**Job:** Suggest safe slippage for a specific swap route.\n\n**Inputs:**\n- `token_in` - Input token address\n- `token_out` - Output token address\n- `amount_in` - Amount to swap\n- `route_hint` - Suggested route/DEX\n\n**Returns:**\n- `min_safe_slip_bps` - Minimum safe slippage in basis points\n- `pool_depths` - Liquidity depth data for route\n- `recent_trade_size_p95` - 95th percentile of recent trade sizes\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n✅ Slippage suggestion prevents revert for 95% of test swaps  \n✅ Accounts for pool depth and recent volatility  \n✅ **Must be deployed on a domain and reachable via x402**\n\n## Done When\nAgent provides slippage recommendations that demonstrably reduce swap failures.\n\n---\n\n## Basic Example\n\n```typescript\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { createAgentApp } from \"@lucid-dreams/agent-kit\";\n\nconst { app, addEntrypoint } = createAgentApp({\n  name: \"slippage-sentinel\",\n  version: \"0.1.0\",\n  description: \"Estimate safe slippage tolerance for any route\",\n});\n\naddEntrypoint({\n  key: \"echo\",\n  description: \"Echo a message\",\n  input: z.object({ text: z.string() }),\n  async handler({ input }) {\n    return {\n      output: { text: String(input.text ?? \"\") },\n      usage: { total_tokens: String(input.text ?? \"\").length },\n    };\n  },\n});\n\nexport default app;\n```\n\n---\n\n## Resources\n- [@lucid-dreams/agent-kit](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@lucid-dreams/agent-kit)\n\n## Submission\n**Submission is a PR into this repo linking the issue - first in first served if the bounty has been completed**","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/issues/3/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/issues/3/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microg/GmsCore/issues/2994","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microg/GmsCore","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microg/GmsCore/issues/2994/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microg/GmsCore/issues/2994/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microg/GmsCore/issues/2994/events","html_url":"https://github.com/microg/GmsCore/issues/2994","id":3284720071,"node_id":"I_kwDOASMt287DyNnH","number":2994,"title":"[BOUNTY] RCS Support [14999$]","user":{"login":"unpluggederan","id":116825601,"node_id":"U_kgDOBvaeAQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116825601?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/unpluggederan","html_url":"https://github.com/unpluggederan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unpluggederan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unpluggederan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unpluggederan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unpluggederan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unpluggederan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unpluggederan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unpluggederan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unpluggederan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unpluggederan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":94622516,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw5NDYyMjUxNg==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microg/GmsCore/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"9C27B0","default":true,"description":null},{"id":431160732,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0MzExNjA3MzI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microg/GmsCore/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"129e5e","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":563,"created_at":"2025-08-01T18:02:52Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:40:14Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Feature Description:**\nGoogle Messages is currently the only widely available RCS client for Android. When attempting to use Google Messages with microG, users typically encounter issues such as:\n\nA persistent message stating \"RCS chats aren't available for this device.\"\nAn indefinite \"Setting up...\", where authentication of the phone number never completes.\n\nRecent developments suggest that Google Messages no longer strictly requires device attestation for RCS, making it possible to enable RCS functionality with microG. However, it appears there's a missing component or necessary adjustment within microG itself preventing successful setup.\n\nGoogle has effectively monopolized RCS, despite it being a GSMA-backed standard intended as a successor to SMS. Unlike SMS, RCS has become a closed ecosystem under Google's control, restricting open interoperability and limiting choice for users and developers. RCS has seen significant adoption, particularly in North America, and recently Apple added support RCS, further increasing its importance as a messaging standard.\n\n**Requested Solution**\n\nProvide a solution that enables Google Messages to successfully connect to and use RCS functionality when operating with microG. Acceptable outcomes include:\n- A fix or enhancement to microG itself, allowing seamless RCS connectivity.\n- Compatibility with recent versions of Google Messages is desired. Solutions that only support a specific Google Messages version from the past year will be awarded half of the bounty amount.\n- Modifications to AOSP or additional permissions changes are acceptable.\n- The solution must work on devices with a locked bootloader.\n\nLimitations\nSolutions relying on rooting, Magisk, or similar root-based tools are not acceptable.\n\n**Additional Information**\n\nGrapheneOS users, who leverage a Play services sandbox, have reported success with enabling RCS by applying permission changes. Although their setup differs from microG, the discussions that were taken in this thread (especially in the last year) may offer valuable insights for this bounty: https://discuss.grapheneos.org/d/1353-using-rcs-with-google-messages-on-grapheneos\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microg/GmsCore/issues/2994/reactions","total_count":70,"+1":35,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":22,"confused":0,"heart":7,"rocket":5,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microg/GmsCore/issues/2994/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/corsairdev/corsair/issues/385","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/corsairdev/corsair","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/corsairdev/corsair/issues/385/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/corsairdev/corsair/issues/385/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/corsairdev/corsair/issues/385/events","html_url":"https://github.com/corsairdev/corsair/issues/385","id":4825950171,"node_id":"I_kwDOQCf-Oc8AAAABH6Yn2w","number":385,"title":"Add LinkedIn integration","user":{"login":"ambikeesshh","id":224122452,"node_id":"U_kgDODVvWVA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224122452?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ambikeesshh","html_url":"https://github.com/ambikeesshh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ambikeesshh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ambikeesshh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ambikeesshh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ambikeesshh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ambikeesshh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ambikeesshh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ambikeesshh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ambikeesshh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ambikeesshh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-07T06:39:52Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:39:52Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**What API or service would you like integrated?**\nLinkedIn\n\n**API documentation link:**\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/linkedin/\n\n**What would you like to do with this integration?**\nPicking this up from the OSS bounty (https://corsair.dev/oss/linkedin). The plugin covers all 22 listed operations across profile, posts, media, comments, organizations/stats, and marketing ads:\n\n- Profile: get my info, get a person by ID\n- Posts: create text post, create article/URL share, get post content, delete via Posts API / shares / UGC endpoints\n- Comments & reactions: create comment, list reactions\n- Media: get image(s), initialize + register image uploads, get videos\n- Organizations: company roles (ACLs), follower count, page statistics, share statistics\n- Ads: targeting facets, audience counts, typeahead entity search\n\n**Do you need webhook support?**\nNo.\n\n**Additional context**\n- Auth: OAuth 2.0 (3-legged) with refresh token handling and rotation\n- Org stats and ads endpoints need Marketing API / organization admin scopes\n- No webhooks on this one","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/corsairdev/corsair/issues/385/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/corsairdev/corsair/issues/385/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/94716","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/Ap