s:\n- Exploitability Metrics:\n  - Attack Vector: Network\n  - Attack Complexity: Low\n  - Privileges Required: None\n  - User Interaction: None\n  - Scope: Unchanged\n- Impact Metrics:\n  - Confidentiality Impact: High\n  - Integrity Impact: High\n  - Availability Impact: None\n</p>\nFor more information on CVSS3 Scores, click <a href=\"https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.0\">here</a>.\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Suggested Fix\n<p>\n\n<p>Type: Upgrade version</p>\n<p>Origin: <a href=\"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2024-53900\">https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2024-53900</a></p>\n<p>Release Date: 2024-12-02</p>\n<p>Fix Resolution: 5.13.23</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n\n:rescue_worker_helmet: Automatic Remediation will be attempted for this issue.\n</details><details>\n\n<summary><img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/critical_vul.png?' width=19 height=20> <img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/viaRed.png' width=19 height=20> CVE-2025-23061</summary>\n\n\n###  Vulnerable Library - <b>mongoose-5.13.14.tgz</b>\n\n<p></p>\n<p>Library home page: <a href=\"https://registry.npmjs.org/mongoose/-/mongoose-5.13.14.tgz\">https://registry.npmjs.org/mongoose/-/mongoose-5.13.14.tgz</a></p>\n<p>Path to dependency file: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json</p>\n<p>Path to vulnerable library: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json</p>\n<p>\n\nDependency Hierarchy:\n  - :x: **mongoose-5.13.14.tgz** (Vulnerable Library)\n<p>Found in HEAD commit: <a href=\"https://github.com/DimaMend/V-Achilles/commit/11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a\">11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a</a></p>\n<p>Found in base branch: <b>master</b></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n### Reachability Analysis\nThis vulnerability is potentially reachable\n\n```\nbaak-dataload-sql-1.0.0/src/models/report.ts (Application)\n  -> mongoose-5.13.14/index.js (Extension)\n   -> mongoose-5.13.14/lib/index.js (Extension)\n    -> mongoose-5.13.14/lib/schema/index.js (Extension)\n     -> ❌ mongoose-5.13.14/lib/schema/array.js (Vulnerable Component)\n\n```\n\n\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Vulnerability Details\n<p>  \n  \nMongoose before 8.9.5 can improperly use a nested $where filter with a populate() match, leading to search injection. NOTE: this issue exists because of an incomplete fix for CVE-2024-53900.\n\n<p>Publish Date: 2025-01-15\n<p>URL: <a href=https://www.mend.io/vulnerability-database/CVE-2025-23061>CVE-2025-23061</a></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Threat Assessment\n<p>  \n\n<p>Exploit Maturity: Not Defined</p>\n<p>EPSS: 7.025%</p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  CVSS 3 Score Details (<b>9.0</b>)\n<p>\n\nBase Score Metrics:\n- Exploitability Metrics:\n  - Attack Vector: Network\n  - Attack Complexity: High\n  - Privileges Required: None\n  - User Interaction: None\n  - Scope: Changed\n- Impact Metrics:\n  - Confidentiality Impact: High\n  - Integrity Impact: High\n  - Availability Impact: High\n</p>\nFor more information on CVSS3 Scores, click <a href=\"https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.0\">here</a>.\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Suggested Fix\n<p>\n\n<p>Type: Upgrade version</p>\n<p>Release Date: 2025-01-15</p>\n<p>Fix Resolution: mongoose -  6.13.6,7.8.4,8.9.5</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n\n:rescue_worker_helmet: Automatic Remediation will be attempted for this issue.\n</details><details>\n\n<summary><img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/high_vul.png?' width=19 height=20> <img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/viaRed.png' width=19 height=20> CVE-2026-42334</summary>\n\n\n###  Vulnerable Library - <b>mongoose-5.13.14.tgz</b>\n\n<p></p>\n<p>Library home page: <a href=\"https://registry.npmjs.org/mongoose/-/mongoose-5.13.14.tgz\">https://registry.npmjs.org/mongoose/-/mongoose-5.13.14.tgz</a></p>\n<p>Path to dependency file: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json</p>\n<p>Path to vulnerable library: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json</p>\n<p>\n\nDependency Hierarchy:\n  - :x: **mongoose-5.13.14.tgz** (Vulnerable Library)\n<p>Found in HEAD commit: <a href=\"https://github.com/DimaMend/V-Achilles/commit/11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a\">11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a</a></p>\n<p>Found in base branch: <b>master</b></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n### Reachability Analysis\nThis vulnerability is potentially reachable\n\n```\nbaak-dataload-sql-1.0.0/src/models/report.ts (Application)\n  -> mongoose-5.13.14/index.js (Extension)\n   -> mongoose-5.13.14/lib/index.js (Extension)\n    -> mongoose-5.13.14/lib/schema/index.js (Extension)\n     -> ❌ mongoose-5.13.14/lib/schema/number.js (Vulnerable Component)\n\n```\n\n\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Vulnerability Details\n<p>  \n  \nMongoose is a MongoDB object modeling tool designed to work in an asynchronous environment. Prior to 6.13.9, 7.8.9, 8.22.1, and 9.1.6, a vulnerability allows bypassing Mongoose’s sanitizeFilter query sanitization mechanism via the $nor operator. When sanitizeFilter is enabled, Mongoose wraps query operators in $eq to neutralize them. However, prior to the fix, $nor was not included in the set of logical operators that are recursively sanitized. Because $nor accepts an array (like $and and $or), and arrays do not trigger hasDollarKeys(), malicious operators such as $ne, $gt, or $regex could be injected inside a $nor clause without being sanitized. This vulnerability is fixed in 6.13.9, 7.8.9, 8.22.1, and 9.1.6.\n\n<p>Publish Date: 2026-05-14\n<p>URL: <a href=https://www.mend.io/vulnerability-database/CVE-2026-42334>CVE-2026-42334</a></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Threat Assessment\n<p>  \n\n<p>Exploit Maturity: Not Defined</p>\n<p>EPSS: 0.274%</p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  CVSS 3 Score Details (<b>7.5</b>)\n<p>\n\nBase Score Metrics:\n- Exploitability Metrics:\n  - Attack Vector: Network\n  - Attack Complexity: Low\n  - Privileges Required: None\n  - User Interaction: None\n  - Scope: Unchanged\n- Impact Metrics:\n  - Confidentiality Impact: High\n  - Integrity Impact: None\n  - Availability Impact: None\n</p>\nFor more information on CVSS3 Scores, click <a href=\"https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.0\">here</a>.\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Suggested Fix\n<p>\n\n<p>Type: Upgrade version</p>\n<p>Origin: <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/mongoose/security/advisories/GHSA-wpg9-53fq-2r8h\">https://github.com/Automattic/mongoose/security/advisories/GHSA-wpg9-53fq-2r8h</a></p>\n<p>Release Date: 2026-05-06</p>\n<p>Fix Resolution: 6.13.9</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n\n:rescue_worker_helmet: Automatic Remediation will be attempted for this issue.\n</details><details>\n\n<summary><img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/high_vul.png?' width=19 height=20> <img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/viaRed.png' width=19 height=20> CVE-2022-2564</summary>\n\n\n###  Vulnerable Library - <b>mongoose-5.13.14.tgz</b>\n\n<p></p>\n<p>Library home page: <a href=\"https://registry.npmjs.org/mongoose/-/mongoose-5.13.14.tgz\">https://registry.npmjs.org/mongoose/-/mongoose-5.13.14.tgz</a></p>\n<p>Path to dependency file: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json</p>\n<p>Path to vulnerable library: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json</p>\n<p>\n\nDependency Hierarchy:\n  - :x: **mongoose-5.13.14.tgz** (Vulnerable Library)\n<p>Found in HEAD commit: <a href=\"https://github.com/DimaMend/V-Achilles/commit/11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a\">11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a</a></p>\n<p>Found in base branch: <b>master</b></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n### Reachability Analysis\nThis vulnerability is potentially reachable\n\n```\nbaak-dataload-sql-1.0.0/src/models/report.ts (Application)\n  -> mongoose-5.13.14/index.js (Extension)\n   -> mongoose-5.13.14/lib/index.js (Extension)\n    -> mongoose-5.13.14/lib/query.js (Extension)\n     -> ❌ mongoose-5.13.14/lib/helpers/query/completeMany.js (Vulnerable Component)\n\n```\n\n\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Vulnerability Details\n<p>  \n  \nPrototype Pollution in GitHub repository automattic/mongoose prior to 6.4.6.\n\n<p>Publish Date: 2022-07-28\n<p>URL: <a href=https://www.mend.io/vulnerability-database/CVE-2022-2564>CVE-2022-2564</a></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Threat Assessment\n<p>  \n\n<p>Exploit Maturity: Not Defined</p>\n<p>EPSS: 32.676%</p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  CVSS 3 Score Details (<b>7.0</b>)\n<p>\n\nBase Score Metrics:\n- Exploitability Metrics:\n  - Attack Vector: Network\n  - Attack Complexity: High\n  - Privileges Required: None\n  - User Interaction: None\n  - Scope: Unchanged\n- Impact Metrics:\n  - Confidentiality Impact: Low\n  - Integrity Impact: Low\n  - Availability Impact: High\n</p>\nFor more information on CVSS3 Scores, click <a href=\"https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.0\">here</a>.\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Suggested Fix\n<p>\n\n<p>Type: Upgrade version</p>\n<p>Origin: <a href=\"https://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2022-2564\">https://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2022-2564</a></p>\n<p>Release Date: 2022-07-28</p>\n<p>Fix Resolution: 5.13.15</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n\n:rescue_worker_helmet: Automatic Remediation will be attempted for this issue.\n</details><details>\n\n<summary><img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/medium_vul.png?' width=19 height=20> <img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/viaRed.png' width=19 height=20> CVE-2025-2306</summary>\n\n\n###  Vulnerable Library - <b>mongoose-5.13.14.tgz</b>\n\n<p></p>\n<p>Library home page: <a href=\"https://registry.npmjs.org/mongoose/-/mongoose-5.13.14.tgz\">https://registry.npmjs.org/mongoose/-/mongoose-5.13.14.tgz</a></p>\n<p>Path to dependency file: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json</p>\n<p>Path to vulnerable library: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json</p>\n<p>\n\nDependency Hierarchy:\n  - :x: **mongoose-5.13.14.tgz** (Vulnerable Library)\n<p>Found in HEAD commit: <a href=\"https://github.com/DimaMend/V-Achilles/commit/11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a\">11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a</a></p>\n<p>Found in base branch: <b>master</b></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n### Reachability Analysis\nThis vulnerability is potentially reachable\n\n```\nbaak-dataload-sql-1.0.0/src/models/report.ts (Application)\n  -> mongoose-5.13.14/index.js (Extension)\n   -> mongoose-5.13.14/lib/index.js (Extension)\n    -> mongoose-5.13.14/lib/model.js (Extension)\n     -> ❌ mongoose-5.13.14/lib/helpers/populate/getModelsMapForPopulate.js (Vulnerable Component)\n\n```\n\n\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Vulnerability Details\n<p>  \n  \nAn Improper Access Control vulnerability was\nidentified in the file download functionality. This vulnerability allows users\nto download sensitive documents without authentication, if the URL is known.\nThe attack\nrequires the attacker to know the documents UUIDv4.\n\n<p>Publish Date: 2025-05-16\n<p>URL: <a href=https://www.mend.io/vulnerability-database/CVE-2025-2306>CVE-2025-2306</a></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Threat Assessment\n<p>  \n\n<p>Exploit Maturity: Not Defined</p>\n<p>EPSS: 0.398%</p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  CVSS 3 Score Details (<b>5.9</b>)\n<p>\n\nBase Score Metrics:\n- Exploitability Metrics:\n  - Attack Vector: Network\n  - Attack Complexity: High\n  - Privileges Required: None\n  - User Interaction: None\n  - Scope: Unchanged\n- Impact Metrics:\n  - Confidentiality Impact: High\n  - Integrity Impact: None\n  - Availability Impact: None\n</p>\nFor more information on CVSS3 Scores, click <a href=\"https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.0\">here</a>.\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Suggested Fix\n<p>\n\n<p>Type: Upgrade version</p>\n<p>Origin: <a href=\"https://securityonline.info/cve-2025-2306-cvss-9-0-mongoose-flaw-leaves-millions-of-downloads-exposed-to-search-injection/\">https://securityonline.info/cve-2025-2306-cvss-9-0-mongoose-flaw-leaves-millions-of-downloads-exposed-to-search-injection/</a></p>\n<p>Release Date: 2025-01-18</p>\n<p>Fix Resolution: mongoose -6.13.6,7.8.4,8.9.5</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n\n:rescue_worker_helmet: Automati