ssues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bounty: 3 RTC\n\n### What You'll Do\nResearch RustChain and compare it to another blockchain project you know.\n\n### Steps\n1. **Pick any other blockchain project**: Bitcoin, Ethereum, Solana, Ergo, Chia, whatever you know\n2. **Write a comparison** (300-800 words) covering:\n   - Consensus mechanism differences (PoW vs PoS vs PoA vs RustChain's Proof of Antiquity)\n   - Hardware requirements\n   - Environmental approach\n   - Community model\n   - What each project does better\n3. **Post as a comment here**\n\n### What Counts\n- Must show you actually read about both projects\n- Honest comparison, it's fine to say where RustChain falls short\n- We learn from your outside perspective\n- Tables/charts welcome but not required\n\n### Payment\n3 RTC for a thoughtful, accurate comparison.\n\n**Difficulty**: Easy-Medium | **Time**: 30-45 min | **Skills**: Research, writing\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2786/reactions","total_count":14,"+1":7,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":3,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2786/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/5","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/5/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/5/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/5/events","html_url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/5","id":4148310877,"node_id":"I_kwDORx6c0M73QjNd","number":5,"title":"[BOUNTY $200] WORKFLOW: n8n + Claude Code — automated weekly dev summary","user":{"login":"claudebounty","id":271393208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEC0huA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271393208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty","html_url":"https://github.com/claudebounty","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10532402505,"node_id":"LA_kwDORx6c0M8AAAACc8e1SQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"D97706","default":false,"description":"Task with financial reward"},{"id":10532402738,"node_id":"LA_kwDORx6c0M8AAAACc8e2Mg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/labels/workflow","name":"workflow","color":"0891B2","default":false,"description":"Automation workflow"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":828,"created_at":"2026-03-27T00:55:44Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T05:01:58Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## 💰 Bounty: $200 — powered by [Opire](https://opire.dev)\n\n## Description\nCreate a complete n8n workflow that automatically generates a weekly narrative\nsummary of a GitHub repo's activity, using the Claude API.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Exportable n8n workflow (importable `.json` file)\n- [ ] Trigger: weekly cron (e.g., Friday at 5pm)\n- [ ] Fetches from GitHub API: commits, closed issues, merged PRs for the week\n- [ ] Calls Claude API (`claude-sonnet-4-20250514`) to generate a narrative summary\n- [ ] Delivers the summary via: email OR Discord/Slack webhook (your choice, documented)\n- [ ] Configurable variables: GitHub repo, destination channel, language (EN/FR)\n- [ ] Tested on a real n8n instance (include a screenshot of successful execution)\n- [ ] README with setup instructions in 5 steps or fewer\n\n## How to Claim\n1. Comment `/opire try` in this issue\n2. Submit a PR with the `.json` workflow + README\n3. Payment is released automatically on merge ✅\n\n## Resources\n- n8n docs: https://docs.n8n.io\n- Claude API docs: https://docs.anthropic.com","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/5/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/5/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/paritytech/web3-storage/issues/177","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/paritytech/web3-storage","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/paritytech/web3-storage/issues/177/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/paritytech/web3-storage/issues/177/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/paritytech/web3-storage/issues/177/events","html_url":"https://github.com/paritytech/web3-storage/issues/177","id":4665751508,"node_id":"I_kwDOQ7EgZs8AAAABFhm31A","number":177,"title":"Scheduling & lazy processing: move unbounded on_finalize work to on_poll / bounded lazy cleanup","user":{"login":"bkontur","id":8159517,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNTk1MTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8159517?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkontur","html_url":"https://github.com/bkontur","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkontur/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkontur/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkontur/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkontur/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkontur/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkontur/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkontur/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkontur/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkontur/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10005529938,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQ7EgZs8AAAACVGBFUg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/paritytech/web3-storage/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or request"},{"id":10863048366,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQ7EgZs8AAAACh3z2rg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/paritytech/web3-storage/labels/architecture","name":"architecture","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":null},{"id":10863050232,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQ7EgZs8AAAACh3z9-A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/paritytech/web3-storage/labels/discussion","name":"discussion","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-06-15T13:57:52Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T05:01:27Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Scheduling & lazy processing\n\nThe design's principle is to **avoid periodic/scheduled on-chain work** (the chain is \"a credible threat, not the hot path\" — explicitly contrasted with Filecoin's per-sector periodic proofs). So almost everything is intentionally pull / event / off-chain. The one thing the design *does* schedule is challenge-timeout slashing, processed at the deadline block.\n\nThe **Implement?** column is validated against the canonical design (#170).\n\n| Concern | Deadline source | Current handling | Implement? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Challenge timeout → slash** | `Challenges[deadline_block]`, `deadline = now + ChallengeTimeout` | `on_finalize(n)` slashes every challenge maturing at block `n` | 🟡 **Keep scheduled (by design); harden only.** Design intends deadline-block processing and considers the batch bounded-by-weight (all challenges at `n` were created at the single block `n − ChallengeTimeout`). Not a design gap. Defensive hardening: make the bound explicit (`BoundedVec`) and consider moving the slashing off `on_finalize` (critical path) to `on_idle`/`on_poll` |\n| **Agreement expiry** (`expires_at`) | per-agreement field | Pull: `end_agreement` (owner) / `claim_expired_agreement` (provider) | ⚠️ **Optional / low.** Pull is by design; only consider cleanup for the residual where neither party acts |\n| **Missed checkpoint → slash** | checkpoint window + grace | Pull + incentivized: `report_missed_checkpoint` (reporter gets 10%) | ❌ **No (works as designed).** 10% reporter reward is canonical; at most document it |\n| **Agreement request expiry** (`RequestTimeout`) | config (6h) | None — only a `// TODO` in `provider-node/src/api.rs:815` | 🟡 **Decision first.** Design↔code divergence: design (#170) keeps on-chain requests with `expires_at`; code (#105) moved negotiation off-chain. Reconcile, then implement lazy expiry only if requests stay on-chain |\n| **Deregistration** | `deregister_at = now + DeregisterAnnouncementPeriod` | Pull: announce → wait → `complete_deregister` | ❌ **No.** Two-phase pull is intended |\n| **Checkpoint rewards** | accrue per (provider, bucket) | Pull: `claim_checkpoint_rewards` | ❌ **No.** Pull claim is fine; keep the accrual map bounded |\n\n**Net:** per the design, nothing *new* needs scheduling. Challenge-timeout slashing is the only chain-scheduled item and is bounded-by-design — worth only defensive hardening. `RequestTimeout` needs a design↔code decision first. Everything else works as designed (pull / off-chain).\n\nNote: per design, challenge-resolution paths must use refund/penalty, never bounties (no challenger reward) — keep that separate from the checkpoint-miss reporter reward.\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/paritytech/web3-storage/issues/177/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/paritytech/web3-storage/issues/177/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devpool-directory/devpool-directory/issues/5925","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devpool-directory/devpool-directory","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devpool-directory/devpool-directory/issues/5925/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devpool-directory/devpool-directory/issues/5925/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devpool-directory/devpool-directory/issues/5925/events","html_url":"https://github.com/devpool-directory/devpool-directory/issues/5925","id":3885310706,"node_id":"I_kwDOJWyCVM7nlSLy","number":5925,"title":"Launch campaign towards L1s/L2s for managing their GitHubs","user":{"login":"devpool-directory-superintendent[bot]","id":179499210,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCrLwyg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/979607?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/devpool-directory-superintendent%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/devpool-directory-superintendent","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devpool-directory-superintendent%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devpool-directory-superintendent%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devpool-directory-superintendent%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devpool-directory-superintendent%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devpool-directory-superintendent%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devpool-directory-superintendent%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devpool-directory-superintendent%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devpool-directory-superintendent%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devpool-directory-superintendent%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9443193576,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJWyCVM8AAAACMtuy6A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devpool-directory/devpool-directory/labels/Priority:%201%20(Normal)","name":"Priority: 1 (Normal)","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":9443193717,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJWyCVM8AAAACMtuzdQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devpool-directory/devpool-directory/labels/Price:%20600%20USD","name":"Price: 600 USD","color":"1f883d","default":false,"description":""},{"id":9443193726,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJWyCVM8AAAACMtuzfg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devpool-directory/devpool-directory/labels/Time